# S76 dogfood: commit only the curated evidence (harness, task, checklist, the 2
# receipts). Raw captures + 285KB transcripts stay LOCAL — the receipts carry the
# authoritative-absent warning + cost lines the report cites.
sessions/session-76-artifacts/*
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/capture.sh
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/task-prompt.txt
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/measurement-checklist.md
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/run1
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/run2
sessions/session-76-artifacts/run1/*
sessions/session-76-artifacts/run2/*
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/run1/receipt.stderr.txt
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/run2/receipt.stderr.txt
# S77 regression fixture — real captured message.usage slice, small + committed (the
# meter/receipt tests + verify-session-77 depend on it; the raw run.jsonl stays local).
!sessions/session-76-artifacts/fixtures

# ── SESSION ARTIFACTS ARE NOT PUSHED (founder call, S126) ───────────────────────────────────────
# A session's raw working evidence — transcripts, run captures, harness scratch, before/after logs
# — stays LOCAL. `sessions/` carries only the small, permanent records: the session summary, the
# cold review, and any short evidence RECORD a verify suite parses (e.g.
# sessions/session-126-dispatch-evidence.md). S126 pushed 1.1 MB of raw JSONL before this rule
# existed; `sessions/` had already grown to 11 MB of a 17 MB repo.
#
# The rule for a verify suite: if a check needs evidence, commit a DERIVED record small enough to
# read (ids, sha256s, costs) and keep the raw file local — the S76/S77 pattern above, now general.
# Already-tracked artifacts from earlier sessions are unaffected (git ignores only untracked
# files); removing those from history is a separate, destructive, founder-gated call.
sessions/session-*-artifacts/
